// TravelMap build configuration.
//
//   cp Config.xcconfig.example Config.xcconfig
//
// then fill in the two values below from your Supabase project's
// Project Settings -> API Keys page. Config.xcconfig is git-ignored; this template is
// not, so never put real keys in this file.
//
// SLASH exists because xcconfig strips "//" as a comment, even mid-value. Splitting the
// URL's separator through a variable is the only form that survives both the xcconfig
// parser and Info.plist preprocessing -- paste your URL around it exactly as shown, and
// leave the "$(SLASH)$(SLASH)" alone.

SLASH = /
SUPABASE_URL = https:$(SLASH)$(SLASH)your-project-ref.supabase.co

// The PUBLISHABLE key -- "sb_publishable_...", or the legacy key labelled "anon".
// It is meant to ship inside a client: Row Level Security is what actually protects
// the data.
//
// Never the secret key ("sb_secret_...", or a legacy "service_role" JWT). That one
// bypasses Row Level Security entirely, and anything shipped in an app binary can be
// read straight out of it. The app checks for this at launch and refuses to start.

SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-publishable-key
